  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    h = len(grid)\n    w = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Find the bounding box of the 5-rectangle\n    rows_5 = [r for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == 5]\n    cols_5 = [c for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c] == 5]\n\n    top = min(rows_5)\n    bottom = max(rows_5)\n    left = min(cols_5)\n    right = max(cols_5)\n\n    # Start with empty grid, then copy the original 5-region\n    out = [[0 for _ in range(w)] for _ in range(h)]\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if grid[r][c] == 5:\n                out[r][c] = 5\n\n    # Horizontal bar: spans full width, extend vertically based on counts per column\n    if left == 0 and right == w - 1:\n        above_counts = [0] * w\n        below_counts = [0] * w\n\n        for r in range(h):\n            for c in range(w):\n                v = grid[r][c]\n                if v != 0 and v != 5:\n                    if r < top:\n                        above_counts[c] += 1\n                    elif r > bottom:\n                        below_counts[c] += 1\n\n        for c in range(w):\n            n = above_counts[c]\n            for k in range(n):\n                rr = top - 1 - k\n                if 0 <= rr < h:\n                    out[rr][c] = 5\n\n            n = below_counts[c]\n            for k in range(n):\n                rr = bottom + 1 + k\n                if 0 <= rr < h:\n                    out[rr][c] = 5\n\n    # Vertical bar: spans full height, extend horizontally based on counts per row\n    elif top == 0 and bottom == h - 1:\n        left_counts = [0] * h\n        right_counts = [0] * h\n\n        for r in range(h):\n            for c in range(w):\n                v = grid[r][c]\n                if v != 0 and v != 5:\n                    if c < left:\n                        left_counts[r] += 1\n                    elif c > right:\n                        right_counts[r] += 1\n\n        for r in range(h):\n            n = left_counts[r]\n            for k in range(n):\n                cc = left - 1 - k\n                if 0 <= cc < w:\n                    out[r][cc] = 5\n\n            n = right_counts[r]\n            for k in range(n):\n                cc = right + 1 + k\n                if 0 <= cc < w:\n                    out[r][cc] = 5\n\n    return out",
